        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Configurable sponsored compute acceptance price",
        "summary": "Added FREEBUFF_SPONSORED_COMPUTE_ACCEPTANCE_PRICE_CENTS env var to override the hardcoded 200-cent acceptance fee. Defaults to 200 when absent; rejects malformed or non-positive integer values by closing admission. Logic moved to sponsoredComputeAcceptancePriceCents in common/src/ads/sponsored-compute-contract.ts. Enforced in readSponsoredComputePolicy before returning the frozen policy object.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T03:37:02.549Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You can now set a custom price (in cents) that someone pays to accept a sponsored compute offer, instead of it always being 200 cents. The price is controlled by a new environment variable; if that variable is missing the price stays at 200 cents, and if the value provided is missing, zero, negative, or not a clean whole number, the system stops accepting the offer entirely rather than guessing. Today the feature is live: any deployment that sets the variable gets the custom price, and any deployment that leaves it unset still gets the original 200-cent fee.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
