      "facts": [
        "The file listing, then one media part per image that was read, so the model sees the picture rather than its bytes decoded as text.",
        "Only hosts that read the workspace locally provide this. Without it, read_files sends image paths through `requestFiles` like any file.",
        "Images skip the text read entirely: decoded as UTF-8 a PNG is a wall of replacement characters, and the model reports \"raw bytes\" instead of describing the picture. A host that cannot read binary leaves them in `requestedFiles`, which keeps its old behavior."
      ],
      "title": "Shared/Core update: read-files",
      "summary": "Shared/Core, Agent Runtime, SDK changes across 8 file(s) (+355/−60).",
      "tags": [
        "sdk"
      ],
      "day": "2026-09-12",
      "month": "2026-09",
      "category": "SDK",
      "significance": "notable",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Read files now attaches images as media instead of reading raw bytes",
        "summary": "The `read_files` tool now detects supported image extensions and, when the host supplies a `requestImageFile` capability, routes image paths to it instead of decoding them as text. The handler emits each image as a media part alongside a `[IMAGE] mediaType, size KB` text entry, while hosts that cannot read binary or use a `read_files` override keep the old text-read behavior. This lets the model see the picture rather than a PNG decoded as replacement characters, and the SDK's new `getImageFile` enforces the same `MAX_IMAGE_READ_BYTES` ceiling, gitignore policy, and missing-file handling as the regular text read.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff adds a `requestImageFile` optional field to `AgentRuntimeScopedDeps` in `common/src/types/contracts/agent-runtime.ts` and the `RequestImageFileFn` type to `common/src/types/contracts/client.ts`. In the `read_files` handler (`packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/read-files.ts`), image paths matching `isImagePath` are now collected into `imagePaths` and skipped from `requestedFiles` when `requestImageFile` is provided, then fetched and emitted as media parts via `mediaToolResult`.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "changes": [
          {
            "area": "common/src/types/contracts/client.ts",
            "what": "Added the `RequestImageFileFn` type and `FileReadWindow` contract for reading an image as base64 with its media type.",
            "files": [
              "common/src/types/contracts/client.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "common/src/types/contracts/agent-runtime.ts",
            "what": "Added optional `requestImageFile` to `AgentRuntimeScopedDeps`, threading it through to the shared deps and SDK runtime.",
            "files": [
              "common/src/types/contracts/agent-runtime.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/read-files.ts",
            "what": "The read_files handler now separates image paths and attaches them as media parts when `requestImageFile` is available, with a fallback that preserves the old text-read path.",
            "files": [
              "packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/read-files.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "sdk/src/tools/read-files.ts",
            "what": "Added `getImageFile` applying the same gitignore, size-limit, and missing-file policy as `getFiles` to image reads, and exported it from the SDK.",
