      "hasDiff": true,
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The cost numbers that get shown for paying subscribers are now defined in one shared place, so every report uses the same labels for what counts as subscription-paid, what is Freebuff-paid, what can't be traced to a funding source, and what the next 30 days are expected to cost. Any part of the system that displays or calculates these costs for a single paying subscriber, a subscription tier, or the whole list will now pull from the same set of fields, including a flag that turns red when any cost in the period can't be tied to who paid for it. The structure is ready for use today, but the reporting screens that would show these numbers are still being built.",
